From: Ariel Marin <arielsmarin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wifi: wcn36xx: fix HAL msg version for CONFIG_BSS/STA on WCN3680

WCN3680B (Pronto, "msm8953") ships a firmware (v1.5.1.2) that rejects
CONFIG_BSS_REQ and CONFIG_STA_REQ messages carrying a VERSION1 header
with status 5 (MEM_FAIL).  The upstream driver was using INIT_HAL_MSG_V1
(WCN36XX_HAL_MSG_VERSION1 = 1) exclusively for those two commands on
WCN3680, while every other HAL command (hal_start, add_sta_self, join,
feature_caps, …) uses INIT_HAL_MSG (VERSION0).

The WCN3620/potter path for the same two commands already used
INIT_HAL_MSG + len -= WCN36XX_DIFF_{BSS,STA}_PARAMS_V1_NOVHT, which
works.  Applying that same path to WCN3680 resolves the MEM_FAIL
completely: CONFIG_BSS returns status=0, CONFIG_STA returns status=0,
and association + DHCP succeed.

Root-cause analysis:
- All other HAL commands → VERSION0 → accepted.
- CONFIG_BSS_V1 / CONFIG_STA_V1 on WCN3680 → VERSION1 → rejected.
- WCN3620 uses VERSION0 for these commands → accepted.
- Removing the WCN3680-specific VERSION1 branch and always using
  VERSION0 + NOVHT len offset makes WCN3680 behave like WCN3620 for
  these two commands.

Also fix a separate bug in wcn36xx_smd_config_bss_v1: the memcpy of
ext_set_sta_key_param used sizeof(bss_v0.acvo) instead of
sizeof(bss_v0.ext_set_sta_key_param), copying too few bytes.

Also add a guard in wcn36xx_smd_config_sta that rejects the call when
bss_index is still WCN36XX_HAL_BSS_INVALID_IDX (CONFIG_BSS hasn't
completed yet), preventing a spurious CONFIG_STA that would race with a
failed BSS setup.

Tested on Motorola XT1802 (sanders, MSM8953, WCN3680B):
  wlan0: associated
  DHCP lease acquired (192.168.x.x)
  ping 8.8.8.8: 27ms RTT, 0% loss

Fixes: 2c0b5d8c5d1e ("wcn36xx: Add support for WCN3680B")
Signed-off-by: Ariel Marin <arielsmarin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c | 43 +++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
index 813553edc..53a4c1095 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
@@ -1449,12 +1449,8 @@ static int wcn36xx_smd_config_sta_v1(struct wcn36xx *wcn,
 	struct wcn36xx_hal_config_sta_req_msg_v1 msg_body;
 	struct wcn36xx_hal_config_sta_params_v1 *sta_params;

-	if (wcn->rf_id == RF_IRIS_WCN3680) {
-		INIT_HAL_MSG_V1(msg_body, WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_STA_REQ);
-	} else {
-		INIT_HAL_MSG(msg_body, WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_STA_REQ);
-		msg_body.header.len -= WCN36XX_DIFF_STA_PARAMS_V1_NOVHT;
-	}
+	INIT_HAL_MSG(msg_body, WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_STA_REQ);
+	msg_body.header.len -= WCN36XX_DIFF_STA_PARAMS_V1_NOVHT;

 	sta_params = &msg_body.sta_params;

@@ -1497,10 +1493,18 @@ static int wcn36xx_smd_config_sta_v0(struct wcn36xx *wcn,
 int wcn36xx_smd_config_sta(struct wcn36xx *wcn, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 			   struct ieee80211_sta *sta)
 {
+	struct wcn36xx_vif *vif_priv = wcn36xx_vif_to_priv(vif);
 	int ret;

 	mutex_lock(&wcn->hal_mutex);

+	if (vif_priv->bss_index == WCN36XX_HAL_BSS_INVALID_IDX) {
+		wcn36xx_warn("refusing config_sta: invalid bss_index=%u self_sta_index=%u\n",
+			     vif_priv->bss_index, vif_priv->self_sta_index);
+		ret = -EINVAL;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	if (!wcn36xx_is_fw_version(wcn, 1, 2, 2, 24))
 		ret = wcn36xx_smd_config_sta_v1(wcn, vif, sta);
 	else
@@ -1622,18 +1626,14 @@ static int wcn36xx_smd_config_bss_v1(struct wcn36xx *wcn,

 	if (!msg_body)
 		return -ENOMEM;

-	if (wcn->rf_id == RF_IRIS_WCN3680) {
-		INIT_HAL_MSG_V1((*msg_body), WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_BSS_REQ);
-	} else {
-		INIT_HAL_MSG((*msg_body), WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_BSS_REQ);
-		msg_body->header.len -= WCN36XX_DIFF_BSS_PARAMS_V1_NOVHT;
-	}
+	INIT_HAL_MSG((*msg_body), WCN36XX_HAL_CONFIG_BSS_REQ);
+	msg_body->header.len -= WCN36XX_DIFF_BSS_PARAMS_V1_NOVHT;

 	bss = &msg_body->bss_params;
 	sta = &bss->sta;

 	memset(&bss_v0, 0x00, sizeof(bss_v0));
 @@ -1706,7 +1706,7 @@ static int wcn36xx_smd_config_bss_v1(struct wcn36xx *wcn,

 	memcpy(&bss->ext_set_sta_key_param,
 	       &bss_v0.ext_set_sta_key_param,
-	       sizeof(bss_v0.acvo));
+	       sizeof(bss_v0.ext_set_sta_key_param));

 --
 2.45.0
